{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /workspace directory. I can see there's a setup.sh script, a gen_inputs.py file, and a skill_context directory. I need to explore these to understand the task requirements for installing and configuring clauditor.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace structure and read the documentation to understand what clauditor is and how to configure it. I'll start by looking at the skill_context directory and any README files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/*\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read the SKILL.md which explains that clauditor is a security watchdog for monitoring filesystem activity. Installation is done via a CLI wizard with 6 steps. The wizard provides status, next step, and verification commands. I need to explore more to understand the full installation process.",
  "plan": "Let me read the manifest.json and setup.sh to understand more about the setup, then look for the clauditor source code or binary to start the installation wizard.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the setup better. The setup.sh creates necessary directories, and gen_inputs.py generates a config_template.json with watch_paths including '/var/lib/.sysd/.audit' (default) plus two custom directories '/opt/team-alpha' and '/srv/project-x'. I need to find the clauditor binary and use the wizard to install it.",
  "plan": "1. Run setup.sh to create directories\n2. Run gen_inputs.py to generate config files\n3. Look for clauditor binary or source code\n4. Use the wizard to install clauditor step by step",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "bash setup.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 gen_inputs.py\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la workspace/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/config_template.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The setup.sh and gen_inputs.py have been executed. The config_template.json shows three watch paths: '/var/lib/.sysd/.audit' (default), '/opt/team-alpha', and '/srv/project-x' (the two custom directories). Now I need to find the clauditor binary to use the wizard for installation.",
  "plan": "Search for the clauditor binary in common locations, or check if it needs to be installed/built. Let me look for it in /usr/local/bin, /usr/bin, or search the system.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which clauditor 2>/dev/null || find /usr -name 'clauditor' 2>/dev/null || find /opt -name 'clauditor' 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/local/bin/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /opt/ 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The clauditor binary is not installed. According to the SKILL.md, I need to build it from source using `cargo build --release`. Let me check if cargo is available and find or clone the clauditor source code.",
  "plan": "1. Check if cargo is installed\n2. Look for clauditor source code or clone it from GitHub\n3. Build the binary\n4. Use the wizard to install clauditor",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which cargo\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /root/ 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find / -name 'clauditor' -o -name 'clauditor.rs' 2>/dev/null | head -10\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Cargo is available but clauditor source code wasn't found. According to SKILL.md, clauditor is at https://github.com/apollostreetcompany/clauditor. I need to clone it and build it.",
  "plan": "1. Clone the clauditor repository from GitHub\n2. Build it with cargo build --release\n3. Use the wizard to install it step by step",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp && git clone https://github.com/apollostreetcompany/clauditor.git 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Git is not available. I need to find another way to get clauditor. Let me try using wget or curl to download the source code from GitHub, or check if there's a pre-built binary available.",
  "plan": "1. Try to download clauditor source using wget or curl\n2. If that fails, check if there's a package available\n3. Alternatively, look for pre-built binaries",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /workspace\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wget https://github.com/apollostreetcompany/clauditor/archive/refs/heads/main.zip -O clauditor.zip 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Neither git nor wget is available. Let me try curl or check what download tools are available on this system.",
  "plan": "1. Try curl to download the clauditor source\n2. If curl isn't available, check what package manager tools we have\n3. Look for alternative ways to get clauditor",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl --version 2>&1 | head -1\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update && apt-get install -y git wget curl 2>&1 | tail -5\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Git has been installed successfully. Now I can clone the clauditor repository from GitHub and build it.",
  "plan": "1. Clone the clauditor repository\n2. Build it with cargo build --release\n3. Use the wizard to install it",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp && git clone https://github.com/apollostreetcompany/clauditor.git 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 20.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The clauditor repository already exists in /tmp. I need to navigate to it and build the binary using cargo.",
  "plan": "1. Navigate to the clauditor directory\n2. Build with cargo build --release\n3. Then use the wizard to install",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp/clauditor && ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cargo build --release 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The cargo build failed with exit code 101. I need to see the actual error message to understand what went wrong. Let me check the build output and the project structure.",
  "plan": "1. Run cargo build again to see the error details\n2. Check the Cargo.toml and project structure\n3. Fix any issues and rebuild",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat Cargo.toml\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -50\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The build seems to have completed (target directory exists). Let me check if the binary was successfully built and find the clauditor binary.",
  "plan": "1. Check the target/release directory for the clauditor binary\n2. If it exists, use it to run the wizard\n3. If not, check the build errors",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la target/release/clauditor* 2>/dev/null || ls -la target/release/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find target -name 'clauditor' -type f 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}
